{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587151-updating-covenant-factions-to-2nd-edition","id":587151,"title":"Updating Covenant factions to 2nd edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-11T08:45:17-07:00","id":587151,"title":"Updating Covenant factions to 2nd edition","content":"is secrets of the covenants going to give us back the factions we got in 1st edition or create all new groups , am a bit nervous on that possiblety<br /> <br /> And wanted to ask for your help in updating them to 2nd edition if we can get confirmation they dont intend to simply update them<br /> <br /> The Amanotsukai, who I admit I love, are a bit conundrum what with their rituals calling for ritual exposure to sunlight with some vampires able to daywalk semi easily, others not able to survive a a second in the sun.<br /> <br /> Another group I find fascinating is the Semiotican's<br /> <br /> Well any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T09:40:19-07:00","id":587194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587151-updating-covenant-factions-to-2nd-edition#post587151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is secrets of the covenants going to give us back the factions we got in 1st edition or create all new groups , am a bit nervous on that possiblety<br /> <br /> And wanted to ask for your help in updating them to 2nd edition if we can get confirmation they dont intend to simply update them<br /> <br /> The Amanotsukai, who I admit I love, are a bit conundrum what with their rituals calling for ritual exposure to sunlight with some vampires able to daywalk semi easily, others not able to survive a a second in the sun.<br /> <br /> Another group I find fascinating is the Semiotican's<br /> <br /> Well any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really that kind of book. It's much more like the clanbooks in presentation. It's also smaller; it fits all five covenants into the one book.<br /> <br /> I know some old factions come up in the fiction. I know some new ones come up as well. I know I tried adding a bunch of implied organisation and structure possibilities into the various mechanics. A lot of that was drawn from 1e faction material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T17:09:05-07:00","id":587523,"title":"","content":"well good to know... any hints on release dates??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T12:43:14-07:00","id":588399,"title":"","content":"The Current Projects page has it projected for this fall. But, as the disclaimer on the page says, the times listed indicate intent, and are not a guarantee. As time progresses, circumstances may interfere with their intent. Details subject to change. <br /> <br /> That's as specific as it gets with any projects until very shortly before the product is released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T13:43:51-07:00","id":589504,"title":"","content":"I was under the Impression that 2ed didn't eliminate any of the pre-existing factions fluff wise. It just called for some homebrewed rule edits for factions which offer merits or devotions that don't quite fit the altered game mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T15:19:05-07:00","id":589595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587151-updating-covenant-factions-to-2nd-edition?p=589504#post589504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the Impression that 2ed didn't eliminate any of the pre-existing factions fluff wise. It just called for some homebrewed rule edits for factions which offer merits or devotions that don't quite fit the altered game mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far i know of nothing that would contradict that impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T16:00:11-07:00","id":589607,"title":"","content":"Nothing was explicitly gotten rid of in 2nd edition beyond those things directly contradicted by the books. So for instance, we can clearly see that the Fog of Eternity is no longer the default situation when a vampire enters torpor, because the book explicitly states otherwise.<br /> <br /> Factions and the Covenant books are slightly trickier. Some of the Covenants have changed slightly in ways that throw some of the factions into question. Some of the mechanics that provided the underlying reason <i>for </i>those factions are no longer present. The Amanotsukai spring to mind as one example. While the mechanic that underpins a lot of their rituals hasn't been removed, it has been sufficiently altered that it might call into question their description.<br /> <br /> Further, there's more radical changes like the origin of the Ordo Dracul, which suggests the idea that it being lead by Dracula and his Wives at any time just never actually happened. <i>That's </i>where you see things more subtly invalidated. Honestly, I think the Ordo is the only one with such a radical change.<br /> <br /> Now, that doesn't mean you can't use the factions, but you should keep your eyes pelled for inconsistencies in descriptions and ideas with regards to the 2e core. <br /> <br /> For my part, I've been adapting factions and ideas, and it's usually pretty easy. It's actually fun when you think about the new, refined focus of Covenants in 2e, and how that can change a faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T17:10:11-07:00","id":590605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587151-updating-covenant-factions-to-2nd-edition?p=589607#post589607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there's more radical changes like the origin of the Ordo Dracul, which suggests the idea that it being lead by Dracula and his Wives at any time just never actually happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula is still credited as &quot;the first Kogaion of the Dragons&quot;, and the Order is organized around the Rites of the Dragon which describes Dracula's brides as the first of the sworn. The line &quot;The Ordo Dracul, without ever gaining his permission, took his name,&quot; in the context of the description of The Rites as &quot;that troublesome hymn to undeath that still circulates tonight among the Kindred&quot;, implies that most chapters of the Ordo organized themselves independently based on the Rites without ever meeting Dracula. Given the relative isolation of Kindred communities from each other, the covenant spreading primarily based on Dracula's &quot;manifesto&quot; makes more sense than it being spread by Vlad himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","user":"Vyrkolash","date":". 07-14-2015, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T14:40:24-07:00","id":593157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587151-updating-covenant-factions-to-2nd-edition?p=590605#post590605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula is still credited as &quot;the first Kogaion of the Dragons&quot;, and the Order is organized around the Rites of the Dragon which describes Dracula's brides as the first of the sworn. The line &quot;The Ordo Dracul, without ever gaining his permission, took his name,&quot; in the context of the description of The Rites as &quot;that troublesome hymn to undeath that still circulates tonight among the Kindred&quot;, implies that most chapters of the Ordo organized themselves independently based on the Rites without ever meeting Dracula. Given the relative isolation of Kindred communities from each other, the covenant spreading primarily based on Dracula's &quot;manifesto&quot; makes more sense than it being spread by Vlad himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in 2ED Dracula wrote his teachings and book spread in the vampires circles to rise as indepentend cults becoming Ordo Dracul we know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:30:22-07:00","id":594024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/587151-updating-covenant-factions-to-2nd-edition?p=593157#post593157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in 2ED Dracula wrote his teachings and book spread in the vampires circles to rise as indepentend cults becoming Ordo Dracul we know?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my reading of the text. The OD book from 1ED makes it clear that for most of it's history the Ordo didn't act as a covenant, rather it spread as a secret society among the Kindred. It wasn't until after the publication of Bram Stoker's Dracula (1897) that Dragons began declaring their membership in the order openly. Prior to 1897 most Dragons were probably members of the Invictus or Lance who kept their OD affiliation and coil research a secret.<br /> <br /> This means Dracula wouldn't show up at Elysium proclaiming, &quot;I'm your new leader, follow me to freedom from the curse&quot; to draw people into the covenant. Instead his writings would be circulated among like minded Kindred with an interest in the occult, who would organize themselves. The 2ED description just emphasizes that dynamic, rather than suggesting there was a formal covenant spreading from Wallachia.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}